 3. 🧽 AI tries to shed toxic branding 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images The great AI rebranding is on, led by President Trump and tech titans like Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, who are embracing an alternative term: "Superintelligence," or SI, Axios' Dave Lawler writes. 

 Why it matters: Leaders in D.C. and Silicon Valley are worried that public backlash against AI and data centers will hamper the development of this staggeringly powerful and existentially dangerous technology. Flanked by the most powerful figures in tech, Trump on Tuesday declared "superintelligence" the preferred terminology of the executive branch. 

 Huang has extended the label to physical infrastructure, referring to data centers as "superintelligence factories." Some of the tech executives who appeared with Trump continued to use "AI" in their remarks. SpaceXAI CEO Elon Musk caught himself and pivoted to "SI." Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg has long used the "superintelligence" branding.

