 7. ✈️ Heroic plumber helped save plane 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Assaf Regavim, one of the passengers who stormed the cockpit to stop the attacking pilot, speaks to reporters outside the terminal at Tel Aviv's Ben Gurion Airport. Photo: Erik Marmor/Getty Images Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu described on CNN how passengers helped rescue a FlyDubai flight bound for Israel that plunged after Capt. Smit Machchhar was stabbed by his co-pilot, Axios' Rebecca Falconer writes. 

 An Israeli passenger who works as a plumber, Yaniv Hayun, entered the cockpit and found the Omani co-pilot at the controls, the Israeli prime minister told CNN's Jim Sciutto. Machchhar had unlocked the cockpit after being attacked. Hayun pulled back on the aircraft's controls, while another passenger and crew member subdued the attacker. Off-duty FlyDubai pilots then took over and stabilized the plane.

 Netanyahu said the attacker, an Omani national, was arrested in Saudi Arabia and was undergoing interrogation there. His motive was unclear. Get the latest . 

 
 
